# Intent: the unit's mute, vision off and full quiet (owner design 2026-11-13, hard mute note). State is three independent bits saved in a NEW NVS namespace maipai_priv (mute, vision, quiet, local_unmute; never the websocket namespace) and restored at boot: the codec is powered down in its constructor before anything can open it. MUTE or QUIET: CoreS3AudioCodec::EnableInput(true) returns at once and Read() hands back paced silence (the audio task reopens the input on its own, so the guard sits inside the codec class), the ES7210 power registers are written by hand and READ BACK (mic_off_verified, with mic_regs), and nothing can arm the wake word or stop word. QUIET also drops all speaker output (Write) and freezes the servos (Servo::update_angle_anim_target and a move under way). VISION OFF: StackChanCamera::Capture and StreamCaptures return false and the avatar socket captures nothing; the minute 'camera' report gains vision_off and vision_skipped. New MCP tools self.privacy.set {mute, vision_off, quiet: -1 leave, 0 off, 1 on} (waits up to 1.5 s for the microphone read-back and answers with the state), self.privacy.get and self.privacy.set_policy {local_unmute}. A 'privacy' event is pushed on every change (source face, home or boot); the minute 'wake_stats' report gains muted, vision_off, quiet and mic_off_verified, so a muted unit can be checked for armed 0, fetches 0 and detections 0.
# Upstream: new files hal/maipai_privacy.h, hal/maipai_privacy.cpp; hal/board/cores3_audio_codec.{h,cc}, stackchan/motion/servo.cpp, hal/board/stackchan_camera.cc, hal/hal_ws_avatar.cpp, hal/hal_head_touch.cpp, hal/hal_mcp.cpp, hal/board/hal_bridge.{h,cc} (MIT). Applies after 105.
# Check after a flash: on a flashed unit, serial log: 'MAIPAI-PRIVACY: saved state: mute=0 ...' at boot; after a mute 'microphone off, read back verified (47:ff,48:ff,49:ff,4a:ff,4b:ff,4c:ff,06:07,01:7f,40:c0)'; if it says NOT verified the registers listed show what the chip really reads, and the mask in CoreS3AudioCodec::MaipaiMicOff needs adjusting (the mute itself still holds). Talk loudly for 30 s while muted: the next wake_stats shows muted=1 armed=0 fetches=0 detections=0 vad_speech=0. Reboot while muted: the unit boots muted (the log says saved state mute=1 and the microphone is never opened).
